# When a user books a taxi in the *Bolt app,* how will the *driver be displayed* : will passengers see an individual taxi driver (like with current Bolt drivers), or will the ride appear as being provided “via ITTaxi”? {color:#ff5630}Yes they won’t see a difference vs. our supply{color}
# Who will be shown as the *service provider* to the passenger:  ITTaxi or the individual driver? {color:#ff5630}ITTaxi will be the provider{color}
# How will *payment* be processed:  through the *Bolt app*, directly to the driver, or through *ITTaxi’s system?* {color:#ff5630}Via the Bolt app like we normally do{color}
# If payment goes through Bolt, how will *settlements* between Bolt and ITTaxi/drivers be handled, and *who issues the receipt* to the passenger? {color:#ff5630}We issue a receipt of the booking/service fee only (like what Uber does), IT Taxi is responsible for issuing a receipt of the ride (the rider needs to ask for it during the ride){color}
# When the ride ends, who triggers the *completion signal* (ITTaxi or Bolt) so that the trip is closed and the fare confirmed? {color:#ff5630}IT Taxi (they will provide all ride data communication once the order is placed){color}
# Finally, will *ITTaxi-affiliated drivers* be required to *accept Bolt’s Terms & Conditions* for service providers, or will their participation be governed solely through ITTaxi’s platform + separate agreement with ITTaxi? {color:#ff5630}yes they will{color}

