Dear [~accountid:712020:a335a5ec-2969-45be-8f2f-6561cf7e7d62]

*We were able to confirm the following:*

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
# In Estonia, Bolt cannot request Estonian criminal record extracts directly from individuals; Bolt must request them from the Estonian criminal records database (Karistusregister).
# Estonian law permits Bolt to seek this information where it deems necessary; it only specifies the conditions under which such checks are mandatory, but those cases are very narrow.
# The prohibition on requesting criminal record extracts directly from individuals, including employees, applies solely to the Karistusregister. Estonian law does not impose any similar restrictions concerning the criminal record databases of other countries. Therefore, for extracts issued by foreign authorities, the laws of the respective countries must be adhered to.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
In other jurisdictions, there may be no restriction preventing individuals from obtaining and submitting their own criminal record extracts, meaning that Bolt’s current practice could be fully compliant with the national laws applicable there.

However, as the rules and procedures differ from country to country, any specific requirements would need to be verified separately for each jurisdiction concerned.
{panel}

*Can you please confirm if you have any remaining questions on the topic?*

