h1. Privacy Assessment 

Is there a valid legal basis for disclosure of Bolt User personal data to the Attorney of the injured party?

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Code*

§ 810 BGB is about inspection of a document

§ 242 BGB is about good-faith performance of obligations
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#ffebe6}
Neither seem to directly grant universal right to the injured party to demand User’s personal data simply because they claim legitimate interest
{panel}



{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Precedents*

Case law cites cases where service provider stores “order data” and an injured party or creditor requests the identity of the service user to pursue a claim. The decisions invoke balancing of interests.

HRC Schleswig of 13 July 2020 – 16 U 137/19 → a service provider storing “order data” may have to disclose user identity if the injured party has a legitimate interest in asserting a civil claim and is dependent on the data
{panel}



